\section{QC checks}{

The 10 checks are:
\enumerate{
\item \strong{Convergence}: Did the model converge?
\item \strong{Global fit}: Infit/Outfit MnSq within the current review band.
\item \strong{Reliability}: Minimum index across explicitly selected differentiation facets.
\item \strong{Separation}: Minimum index across those same selected facets.
\item \strong{Element misfit}: Percentage of elements with Infit/Outfit
outside the current review band.
\item \strong{Unexpected responses}: Percentage of observations with
large standardized residuals.
\item \strong{Category structure}: Minimum category count and threshold
ordering.
\item \strong{Connectivity}: All observations in a single connected subset.
\item \strong{Inter-rater agreement}: Exact agreement percentage for the
rater facet (if applicable).
\item \strong{Functioning/Bias screen}: Percentage of interaction cells that
cross the screening threshold (if interaction results are available).
}
}

\section{Interpreting output}{

\itemize{
\item \verb{$overall}: character string \code{"Pass"}, \code{"Warn"}, or \code{"Fail"}.
\item \verb{$verdicts}: tibble with columns \code{Check}, \code{Verdict}, \code{Value}, and
\code{Threshold} for each of the 10 checks.
\item \verb{$verdicts$Detail}: human-readable explanation of each assessment.
\item \verb{$verdicts$AffectsOverall}: whether a check contributes to the overall result.
\item \verb{$details}: named list of per-check numeric details for programmatic access.
\item \verb{$recommendations}: character vector of actionable suggestions for
checks that need review; suggestions do not prescribe deleting raters or
collapsing categories automatically.
\item \verb{$config}: records the threshold profile and effective thresholds.
}
}

\section{Typical workflow}{

\enumerate{
\item Fit a model: \code{fit <- fit_mfrm(...)}.
\item Optionally compute diagnostics and bias:
\code{diag <- diagnose_mfrm(fit)};
\code{bias <- estimate_bias(fit, diag, ...)}.
\item Run the pipeline: \code{qc <- run_qc_pipeline(fit, diag, bias_results = bias)}.
\item Check \code{qc$overall} for the headline verdict.
\item Review \code{qc$verdicts} for per-check details.
\item Follow \code{qc$recommendations} for remediation.
\item Visualize with \link[=plot.mfrm_qc_pipeline]{plot(x)}.
}
}

\section{Saved-result reuse}{

Supplied screening results must describe this fitted analysis. Results from
another fit or older results without identity metadata are refused. See
\link{mfrmr_compatibility_layer} to recreate them from the saved fit and matching
diagnostics without refitting the model.
}

\section{Interpretation}{

The rows are the actual checks returned by \code{\link[=run_qc_pipeline]{run_qc_pipeline()}}: convergence,
global fit, selected-facet reliability and separation, element misfit,
unexpected responses, category structure, connectivity, inter-rater
agreement, and the functioning/bias screen. Element misfit uses the
configured mean-square band; it is not a ZSTD test. PCA and displacement
are separate diagnostics and are not checks in this pipeline.

Green (Pass), amber (Warn), and red (Fail) describe the selected screening
rules. Grey (Skip) marks unrequested or unavailable checks; \code{AffectsOverall}
in the returned data distinguishes their contribution to the overall result.
A missing result is not evidence of acceptable fit. High rater separation
is not high agreement, and no colour establishes statistical validity or
justifies deleting raters or collapsing categories without further review.
}

